WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:01.790
It's not just about where you're from.

00:00:01.790 --> 00:00:04.130
It's about the changes that you are

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:06.080
very adamant about making from the

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:07.380
place that you grew up in.

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.910
You're very serious about your culture.

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:12.890
You're very serious about uplifting and

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:16.190
creating opportunities for your people,

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:17.570
especially in the place that you come

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:18.710
from. Right?

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:20.110
I want to see change here.

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:21.830
Was that a thing that was always there?

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:24.290
The I want to see change here was the

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:25.850
thing that was always there for me

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:27.260
initially because I didn't know any

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.270
better. It came from in front of the

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:30.980
camera. It came from like the images

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:32.810
that I wanted to see just because I had

00:00:32.810 --> 00:00:34.400
I had seen them. I had grown up on

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:35.930
them. So I knew it was possible.

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:37.490
And so then when it was taken away,

00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:38.930
when I was watching TV in like high

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:41.180
school and college, movies, I was like,

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:42.830
Where's all this stuff that I grew up

00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:44.360
on? Like, you know, where are these

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:46.580
stories? And why is it just kind of the

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:48.530
same narrative that's being shown?

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:49.970
I know we're more than this.

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:52.940
And so like even creating was born out

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:54.860
of a frustration. And then when I did

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:56.630
that online and started making the

00:00:56.630 --> 00:00:57.860
content, I was like, Oh, there are all

00:00:57.860 --> 00:00:59.060
these other jobs.

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:01.800
And initially, it just came out from my

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:03.510
circle. These are the people I know.

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:06.090
And so they're helping me to make this.

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:07.830
They happen to be black because most of

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:09.120
my friends are black.

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:11.370
And then, you know, then by extension,

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:12.660
we were bringing on, you know, more

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:13.890
diverse crew.

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:16.710
And then then it wasn't until I would

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:19.920
work on for smaller things, other sets,

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:21.540
and I'd be like, D***, this is like.

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:24.780
I didn't realize how rare this is to

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:26.830
work with other people of color.

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:29.670
Like Hollywood is very, very white

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:31.320
behind the camera. And so then it

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:33.960
became like, well, if I get my own

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:36.000
show, like I still want to replicate

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:39.060
this because I see that it's a rarity.

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:40.530
And why not?

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:41.160
Because I can.

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:42.240
How did you figure it out, though? How

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:44.820
did you figure out the the development

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:46.350
space of Awkward Black Girl?

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:48.360
Like you said, you came up, you wanted

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:49.350
to act. You knew that that's what you

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:51.420
wanted to do. But a lot of people

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:53.430
struggle with, well, what's my entry?

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:54.980
You are a hot commodity.

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:57.900
Just in the next version of a thing.

00:01:57.900 --> 00:02:00.570
This girl is a star.

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:02.250
Like, Oh, my God, you got to watch this

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:05.400
girl. Like, creating that and then

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:07.140
developing that. Like, where did that

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:08.340
understanding come from? Was that

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:09.860
college that gave you that knowledge?

00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:11.850
Yeah, a little bit. I mean, not for

00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:14.490
myself in particular, but like people

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:15.570
don't know about Awkward Black Girl was

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:17.280
like the third web series that I made.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:19.740
It was the third attempt, and it's the

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:21.490
only one that I was in the first two

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:23.410
that I made, you know, I wrote and

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:25.000
directed them, edited them, all those

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.080
things, you know, that you're doing

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:27.430
when you're making online content

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:29.560
yourself. And, you know, the first one

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:31.480
I did do in college and that was

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:34.390
starring my friends and I loved the

00:02:34.390 --> 00:02:36.730
response that that got just from

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:38.170
college to college.

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:39.940
And, you know, it was about being black

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:41.920
at Stanford called Dorm Diaries.

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:43.930
And that was like, oh, okay.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:45.970
I made something that people like and

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:47.830
it's spreading beyond my friend group.

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:48.880
This is dope.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:50.980
And I just made it online.

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:53.120
And then I still wanted to sell it to

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:55.040
TV. So I was trying to, like, reach

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:57.320
into my network to be like, Hey, I made

00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:58.460
this show. People really like it

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:00.680
online. It's only like 500 to 1000

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:02.600
people. But you know, it's something.

00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:04.400
And they didn't want it.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:06.530
So then I created my second show after

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:08.000
that, and it was starring my brother

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.020
and his friend group.

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:10.460
And that was something that I took more

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:12.020
seriously online where I was like, I'm

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:13.700
gonna release it every week and build a

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:15.590
following there. And I started to learn

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:18.080
the tools of like, you know, you can't

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:19.610
make content that's too long online.

00:03:19.610 --> 00:03:20.870
You have to catch people's attention,

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:21.710
you have to build it, you have to be

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:23.690
consistent. So I started developing

00:03:23.690 --> 00:03:25.730
those skills. So by the time I did

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:26.960
Awkward Black Girl.

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:29.690
And put myself in it, even though I was

00:03:29.690 --> 00:03:31.220
scared as hell to put myself in it.

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:33.170
Well, why why didn't you put yourself in

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:33.860
the other ones?

00:03:34.130 --> 00:03:36.170
Well, by that time, I was just like, I

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:37.820
like to write and direct because I had

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:40.460
gone to a school that that, you know,

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:41.920
like the plays and stuff where I'd have

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:43.310
been. I went to a predominantly black

00:03:43.310 --> 00:03:44.330
and Latino high school.

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:45.680
So like the plays were for us.

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:48.050
I was in all of those by the time I got

00:03:48.050 --> 00:03:49.160
to college. It was a predominantly

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:51.080
white college like there are no roles.

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:52.490
They weren't making stuff for us, so I

00:03:52.490 --> 00:03:54.080
had no interest in the same way.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:56.840
And so it came like my directing and

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:59.210
writing came from like, Oh, I'm gonna

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:01.640
make it. I will create like a play that

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:03.350
features us or whatever it is.

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:04.610
And so by the time Awkward Black Girl

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:07.700
came around, I didn't want to feature

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:09.770
myself because I didn't have the same

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:11.270
confidence anymore. I've been working

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:14.180
with actors and also, you know, I had

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:15.500
someone else in mind like I wrote it

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:17.930
with somebody else in mind, and then

00:04:17.930 --> 00:04:19.820
that person couldn't do it because she

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:21.020
was in law school.

00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:23.150
I was in LA, she was in D.C.

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:25.250
and so I just felt like I was running

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:26.420
out of time. So I was like, Let.

00:04:26.420 --> 00:04:27.200
So you said f*** it, i'll do it.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:27.710
Yeah.

